WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.660
NARRATOR: The
grazing animals must

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:06.973
struggle mightily in search
of a few blades of grass.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.010
Many elk grow weak
as winter drags on,

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.713
but someone else grows strong.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.216
The wolf thrives in winter.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.785
Highly intelligent
and social creatures,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:23.223
they often show a deep
affection for one another.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.392
Their intense family
ties also make

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:28.762
them a deadly hunting unit.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.531
Once completely
exterminated from the park,

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:34.734
gray wolves were
reintroduced in 1995

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.705
and have become a vital player
in the park's ecosystem.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.975
Eagerly chasing a big
bull elk, the wolf is

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.277
in its element in Yellowstone.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:50.417
[tense music]

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.546
But this bull didn't earn his
rank by being anyone's fool.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.189
He finds refuge in the
frigid Lamar River,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.991
where the wolves
cannot follow, and aims

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.626
his impressive rack at them.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.875
[howling]

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.912
But another dinner awaits, as
the rest of the pack announces.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.352
They've taken a weakened
bison during the night,

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:02.388
and there's more than
enough to go around.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.325
With such a large pack to
feed, they need to hunt

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.727
successfully nearly every day.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:12.332
[music playing]

